WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
Put one drop of water on your fingertip.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.030
It has a mass of about
a twentieth of a gram.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.890
Barely anything at all.

4
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:13.750
Yet it is made entirely of water
molecules, each one far too small to see.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.390
So how many water molecules
are in a single drop?

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.170
Could anyone even count them?

7
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.850
In this mission, you'll meet the mole:

8
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.750
the chemist's way of counting
particles by weighing them.

9
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.270
You'll work out relative formula masses,

10
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.410
and move between mass, moles
and numbers of particles.

11
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.240
Your mission: count the molecules
in a single drop of water.
